1
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Dark Prism is a horror, comedy, fantasy film directed by Dylan Mars Greenberg.

2
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Three women with mysterious pasts, a nerdy boy, a company man, and Jesus Christ himself all plunge into an
absurdist nightmare when a giant and magical prism descends upon planet Earth and warps reality.

3
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Featuring Lloyd Kaufman, Blondie's Matt Katz-Bohen, and a
special appearance by indie superstar Mac DeMarco.

4
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Margaret East, played by Sofe Cote.

5
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Jesus Christ, played by Chandani Smith.

6
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:36,000
May West, played by Sara Kaiser.

7
00:30:55,000 --> 00:31:01,000
Caleb / The Information Man, played by Max Husten.

8
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:26,000
Elmer East, played by Robert Prichard.

9
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:51,000
Barnaby, played by Fritz Donnelly.

10
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:16,000
The Dark Crystal is a 1982 dark fantasy film directed by Jim Henson and Frank Oz, produced by Gary
Kurtz and Henson, with a screenplay by David Odell based on a story conceived by Henson.

11
00:48:35,000 --> 00:48:41,000
The film was produced and financed by ITC Entertainment and The Jim
Henson Company and distributed by Universal Pictures.

12
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
It features the voices of Stephen Garlick, Lisa Maxwell,
Billie Whitelaw, Percy Edwards, and Barry Dennen.

13
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:31,000
Set on a fictional planet, the film revolves around Jen and Kira, two Gelflings on a quest to restore balance to
the world of Thra and overthrow the evil, ruling Skeksis by restoring a powerful broken Crystal.

14
01:01:50,000 --> 01:01:56,000
The film was promoted as the first major live-action motion picture without any human actors, featuring
characters realized through groundbreaking animatronics created by Jim Henson's Creature Shop.

15
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:21,000
Many creatures, such as the Gelflings, required as many as four
puppeteers to achieve full movement and expression.

16
01:10:40,000 --> 01:10:46,000
In addition to directing, Henson and Oz also performed several characters alongside regular
Muppets collaborators Kathryn Mullen, Dave Goelz, Steve Whitmire, and Louise Gold.

17
01:15:05,000 --> 01:15:11,000
The primary concept artist was fantasy illustrator Brian Froud, famous for his distinctive fairy and dwarf
designs; Froud later collaborated with Henson on his subsequent fantasy film Labyrinth (1986).

18
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:36,000
The film score was composed by Trevor Jones.

19
01:23:55,000 --> 01:24:01,000
The Dark Crystal initially received mixed reviews from mainstream critics; while being criticized for its darker, more dramatic
tone in contrast to Henson's previous works, it was praised for its narrative, production design, and characters.

20
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:26,000
Over the years, it has been re-evaluated by critics
and has garnered a cult following.

21
01:32:45,000 --> 01:32:51,000
An Emmy Award-winning prequel television series, The Dark Crystal: Age of
Resistance, premiered on Netflix in 2019 and ran for one season.

22
01:37:10,000 --> 01:37:16,000
The film explores themes of psychotronic, digital,
queer, low budget, low-budget filmmaking.

23
01:41:35,000 --> 01:41:41,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
